From d1639a92a94fc769d14e83a0cddb07f6dcb4787c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 08:45:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 095/104] feat(onnxruntime): serve image-classification models
 on /v1/images/classify

ort-server serves POST /classify/image with tflite-server's contract for a
model.onnx or model.ort directory whose manifest.json declares the
image-classification task. The onnxruntime backend now detects that layout
with the shared classifier helper (a directory with both graphs is still one
model), refuses a label/layout mismatch at load, answers the wrong route
with 400, and forwards images like tflite and executorch. The /health
version and truncation warning is about text input, so it runs for text
models only. The descriptor adds the image-classification mode.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
